      "content": "Changing `std::forward<Args>(args)...` to `args...` alters forwarding semantics. Inside `updateLinkSubs`, the args are used across multiple loop iterations, so if a caller passes an rvalue reference, `std::forward` on the first iteration could move-from it, leaving it invalid for subsequent iterations. Passing `args...` (lvalue) here is actually the safer choice for a loop. This looks intentional and correct — but please confirm the Args are cheap-to-copy or references, otherwise each iteration copies. If they are expensive-to-copy types, consider capturing as `const auto&` locals before the loop."
